<title>UK: NW Europe oil, gas rigs down in week - Andersen.</title>
<headline>NW Europe oil, gas rigs down in week - Andersen.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs in operation offshore northwest Europe fell by three rigs to 57 in the week to October 23, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>There were 26 rigs active in U.K. waters, down five, but Norwegian activity was up six at 18.</p>
<p>In the Dutch sector, there were eight rigs active, down one on the week, while Danish and Irish activity was steady at four rigs and one rig respectively.</p>
<p>Onshore drilling activity was unchanged at five rigs, four in the U.K. and one in the Faroe Islands.</p>
<p>--London newsroon, +44 171 542 6280.</p>
</text>
